.TH EUCLID-CLI-EQS-UPDATE-MESSAGE-BODY 1 "November 2026" "euclid-cli 2.1.3" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eqs-update-message-body \- replace the body of a queued message
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eqs update-message-body
.BR \-\-message\-id | \-m
.I MESSAGE-ID
.BR \-\-body | \-b
.I BODY
.SH DESCRIPTION
Replaces the body of a message already on a queue. The whole body is
replaced, not part of it.
.PP
The message keeps its ID, status, priority, visibility and attributes;
only the body, its size and its content type change. The queue's maximum
message length applies as it does to
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-send-message (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-message\-id " " \fIMESSAGE-ID\fR
ID of the message to change. Required.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-body " " \fIBODY\fR
The new body. Required. A value starting with
.I file://
is read from the file it names instead of being taken literally, which is
how a body that does not fit on a command line is given.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The body was replaced. The message ID, the queue, the new size, the size
it replaced and the new content type are printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, no message
with that ID exists, or the new body is longer than the queue allows.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eqs update-message-body \e
    --message-id 6f1b1e2e-... --body '{"orderId":4711,"status":"corrected"}'

euclid-cli eqs update-message-body \e
    --message-id 6f1b1e2e-... --body file://./corrected.json
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eqs (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-get-message (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-list-messages (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-send-message (1)
